# {{ spec.name }} Mobile App - Agent Briefing

> Instructions for AI coding agents (Windsurf Cascade, Kilo CLI, etc.)
> Client lane rules: `.windsurf/rules/mobile-app/80-mobile.md`. Backend (python-api,
> self-hosted Pattern-A auth) rules: `10-python.md`, `30-ops.md`, `55-observability.md`.

## Stack (Expo SDK 55, New Architecture)

- **Expo SDK 55** managed workflow, React 19, React Native 0.81 — New Architecture
  (Fabric/JSI) is mandatory; never write legacy-bridge-dependent code.
- **Navigation:** React Navigation v7 (`@react-navigation/native` + native-stack;
  add bottom-tabs for top-level destinations).
- **Server state:** TanStack React Query (`src/lib/queryClient.ts`) — never call the
  API from a screen; wrap it in a typed hook.
- **Storage:** `react-native-mmkv` for fast non-sensitive KV; `expo-secure-store` for
  JWTs/tokens (never MMKV/AsyncStorage). See `src/lib/storage.ts`.
- **i18n:** `i18next` + `expo-localization` (en, tr from day 1) — `src/lib/i18n.ts`.
  No hardcoded user-facing strings.
- **Crash reporting:** `@sentry/react-native` — `src/lib/sentry.ts` (DSN via
  `EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`).
- **Styling:** `StyleSheet.create` + Ocoron tokens (`src/theme/tokens.ts`) — no raw
  hex in components. Upgrade to `react-native-unistyles` for dynamic theming.
- **Billing:** RevenueCat (see `81-mobile-billing.md`).

## Mandatory Workflow

```bash
python scripts/final_gate.py    # before any commit
```

## Build & Test

```bash
npm install
npm start                       # expo start (Metro)
npm run ios                     # expo run:ios   (dev build; macOS)
npm run android                 # expo run:android (dev build)
npm run typecheck               # tsc --noEmit
npm test                        # jest-expo
npm run lint
npx expo export --platform ios  # verify the JS bundle builds (CI-friendly)
```

**Production binaries: EAS only** — `eas build --profile production` (iOS + Android).
Profiles live in `eas.json` (development / preview / production). No local
Xcode/Android-Studio release builds. Submit via `eas submit`.

> First EAS build needs `assets/icon.png` + a splash (template ships no binaries),
> and an EAS `projectId` in `app.json` (`eas init`).

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── App.tsx           # Providers: Sentry → SafeArea → React Query → Navigation
├── lib/              # i18n, queryClient, sentry, storage (MMKV + secure-store)
├── theme/            # Ocoron design tokens
├── locales/          # en.json, tr.json (source-of-truth strings)
├── navigation/       # React Navigation stacks/tabs + type-safe param lists
└── features/         # Feature-based modules (e.g. files/: screens, hooks, services)
```

## Internal Audit (Mobile-Specific)

- [ ] **Strict typing:** navigation params + API responses explicitly typed.
- [ ] **Hook isolation:** screen logic in custom hooks (e.g. `useFileUpload`).
- [ ] **No web DOM** (`<div>`/`<span>`): React Native primitives only.
- [ ] **`FlatList`/`FlashList`** for dynamic lists — never `<ScrollView>` + `.map()`.
- [ ] **JWTs in `expo-secure-store`**, never MMKV/AsyncStorage.
- [ ] **No hardcoded strings** — run `python scripts/validate_i18n.py`.
- [ ] **No raw hex** — use `src/theme/tokens.ts`.

## One-Test Rule Example

```markdown
## One-Test Rule

**Why:** The biggest risk is a broken bundle / native module mismatch.

**Contract:**
- **Given:** a fresh clone with the current package.json
- **When:** the agent runs `npx expo export --platform ios`
- **Then:** it must produce a valid JS bundle with no resolution/type errors
- **Mocked:** native hardware APIs (camera, GPS)
- **Real:** Metro bundler, TypeScript compiler, Expo CLI
```

## Conventions

- **Feature-based modules:** related code together in `src/features/*`.
- **Type-safe navigation:** routes in `src/navigation/types.ts`.
- **Custom hooks:** extract complex logic from screens (max ~200 lines/screen).
- **No hardcoded secrets:** `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` for client-safe config only.
